[
  {
    "index": 0,
    "dialogueIndex": 0,
    "rawLine": 12,
    "type": "dialogue",
    "speaker": "ALEX",
    "voice": "M1",
    "text": "Welcome to the final episode of Claude Code Mastery. I'm Alex, and it's been a journey getting here.",
    "chapter": "INTRO (3 minutes)",
    "file": "0000.mp3",
    "duration": 6.618,
    "startTime": 0
  },
  {
    "index": 1,
    "dialogueIndex": 1,
    "rawLine": 14,
    "type": "dialogue",
    "speaker": "JAMIE",
    "voice": "F1",
    "text": "I'm Jamie, and wow, we've covered so much. From installation to MCP servers. I feel like a completely different developer than when we started.",
    "chapter": "INTRO (3 minutes)",
    "file": "0001.mp3",
    "duration": 9.822,
    "startTime": 6.618
  },
  {
    "index": 2,
    "dialogueIndex": 2,
    "rawLine": 16,
    "type": "dialogue",
    "speaker": "ALEX",
    "voice": "M1",
    "text": "That's the goal. Today we're synthesizing everything into a cohesive workflow. Best practices, productivity tips, and how to keep improving with Claude Code.",
    "chapter": "INTRO (3 minutes)",
    "file": "0002.mp3",
    "duration": 10.17,
    "startTime": 16.44
  },
  {
    "index": 3,
    "dialogueIndex": 3,
    "rawLine": 24,
    "type": "dialogue",
    "speaker": "JAMIE",
    "voice": "F1",
    "text": "Let's start with daily routine. How do you actually use Claude Code day to day?",
    "chapter": "SEGMENT 1: THE DAILY WORKFLOW (5 minutes)",
    "file": "0003.mp3",
    "duration": 5.224,
    "startTime": 26.61
  },
  {
    "index": 4,
    "dialogueIndex": 4,
    "rawLine": 26,
    "type": "dialogue",
    "speaker": "ALEX",
    "voice": "M1",
    "text": "I start every coding session by launching Claude Code in my project directory. First thing I do is get oriented. \"What did I change yesterday?\" or \"remind me where I left off.\"",
    "chapter": "SEGMENT 1: THE DAILY WORKFLOW (5 minutes)",
    "file": "0004.mp3",
    "duration": 12.678,
    "startTime": 31.835
  },
  {
    "index": 5,
    "dialogueIndex": 5,
    "rawLine": 28,
    "type": "dialogue",
    "speaker": "JAMIE",
    "voice": "F1",
    "text": "Using Claude as memory.",
    "chapter": "SEGMENT 1: THE DAILY WORKFLOW (5 minutes)",
    "file": "0005.mp3",
    "duration": 1.95,
    "startTime": 44.513
  },
  {
    "index": 6,
    "dialogueIndex": 6,
    "rawLine": 30,
    "type": "dialogue",
    "speaker": "ALEX",
    "voice": "M1",
    "text": "Exactly. Then I review my tasks for the day and often ask Claude to help me break them down. \"Here's what I need to accomplish. Let's create a plan.\"",
    "chapter": "SEGMENT 1: THE DAILY WORKFLOW (5 minutes)",
    "file": "0006.mp3",
    "duration": 10.379,
    "startTime": 46.463
  },
  {
    "index": 7,
    "dialogueIndex": 7,
    "rawLine": 32,
    "type": "dialogue",
    "speaker": "JAMIE",
    "voice": "F1",
    "text": "Planning with Claude.",
    "chapter": "SEGMENT 1: THE DAILY WORKFLOW (5 minutes)",
    "file": "0007.mp3",
    "duration": 1.741,
    "startTime": 56.842
  },
  {
    "index": 8,
    "dialogueIndex": 8,
    "rawLine": 34,
    "type": "dialogue",
    "speaker": "ALEX",
    "voice": "M1",
    "text": "As I work, Claude is my constant companion. Reading code, making edits, running tests. When I finish a logical unit, I ask Claude to commit with a good message.",
    "chapter": "SEGMENT 1: THE DAILY WORKFLOW (5 minutes)",
    "file": "0008.mp3",
    "duration": 11.285,
    "startTime": 58.584
  },
  {
    "index": 9,
    "dialogueIndex": 9,
    "rawLine": 36,
    "type": "dialogue",
    "speaker": "JAMIE",
    "voice": "F1",
    "text": "Integrated throughout.",
    "chapter": "SEGMENT 1: THE DAILY WORKFLOW (5 minutes)",
    "file": "0009.mp3",
    "duration": 1.811,
    "startTime": 69.869
  },
  {
    "index": 10,
    "dialogueIndex": 10,
    "rawLine": 38,
    "type": "dialogue",
    "speaker": "ALEX",
    "voice": "M1",
    "text": "And at the end of the day, sometimes I ask Claude to summarize what we accomplished. Good for standups and keeping track of progress.",
    "chapter": "SEGMENT 1: THE DAILY WORKFLOW (5 minutes)",
    "file": "0010.mp3",
    "duration": 9.125,
    "startTime": 71.68
  },
  {
    "index": 11,
    "dialogueIndex": 11,
    "rawLine": 46,
    "type": "dialogue",
    "speaker": "JAMIE",
    "voice": "F1",
    "text": "With Claude doing so much, how do you stay in control?",
    "chapter": "SEGMENT 2: STAYING IN CONTROL (4 minutes)",
    "file": "0011.mp3",
    "duration": 3.553,
    "startTime": 80.805
  },
  {
    "index": 12,
    "dialogueIndex": 12,
    "rawLine": 48,
    "type": "dialogue",
    "speaker": "ALEX",
    "voice": "M1",
    "text": "First, always understand what Claude is doing. Don't approve changes you don't understand. If you're confused, ask Claude to explain.",
    "chapter": "SEGMENT 2: STAYING IN CONTROL (4 minutes)",
    "file": "0012.mp3",
    "duration": 8.777,
    "startTime": 84.358
  },
  {
    "index": 13,
    "dialogueIndex": 13,
    "rawLine": 50,
    "type": "dialogue",
    "speaker": "JAMIE",
    "voice": "F1",
    "text": "No blind approval.",
    "chapter": "SEGMENT 2: STAYING IN CONTROL (4 minutes)",
    "file": "0013.mp3",
    "duration": 1.811,
    "startTime": 93.135
  },
  {
    "index": 14,
    "dialogueIndex": 14,
    "rawLine": 52,
    "type": "dialogue",
    "speaker": "ALEX",
    "voice": "M1",
    "text": "Second, work incrementally. Small changes, frequent commits. If something goes wrong, you can easily revert.",
    "chapter": "SEGMENT 2: STAYING IN CONTROL (4 minutes)",
    "file": "0014.mp3",
    "duration": 7.523,
    "startTime": 94.946
  },
  {
    "index": 15,
    "dialogueIndex": 15,
    "rawLine": 54,
    "type": "dialogue",
    "speaker": "JAMIE",
    "voice": "F1",
    "text": "Small steps.",
    "chapter": "SEGMENT 2: STAYING IN CONTROL (4 minutes)",
    "file": "0015.mp3",
    "duration": 1.463,
    "startTime": 102.47
  },
  {
    "index": 16,
    "dialogueIndex": 16,
    "rawLine": 56,
    "type": "dialogue",
    "speaker": "ALEX",
    "voice": "M1",
    "text": "Third, trust but verify. Run your tests after Claude makes changes. Check the output. Don't assume correctness.",
    "chapter": "SEGMENT 2: STAYING IN CONTROL (4 minutes)",
    "file": "0016.mp3",
    "duration": 7.872,
    "startTime": 103.933
  },
  {
    "index": 17,
    "dialogueIndex": 17,
    "rawLine": 58,
    "type": "dialogue",
    "speaker": "JAMIE",
    "voice": "F1",
    "text": "Verify results.",
    "chapter": "SEGMENT 2: STAYING IN CONTROL (4 minutes)",
    "file": "0017.mp3",
    "duration": 1.533,
    "startTime": 111.804
  },
  {
    "index": 18,
    "dialogueIndex": 18,
    "rawLine": 60,
    "type": "dialogue",
    "speaker": "ALEX",
    "voice": "M1",
    "text": "And fourth, know when to do it yourself. Sometimes you know exactly what to type and it's faster to just do it. Claude is a tool, not a replacement for your skills.",
    "chapter": "SEGMENT 2: STAYING IN CONTROL (4 minutes)",
    "file": "0018.mp3",
    "duration": 10.379,
    "startTime": 113.337
  },
  {
    "index": 19,
    "dialogueIndex": 19,
    "rawLine": 62,
    "type": "dialogue",
    "speaker": "JAMIE",
    "voice": "F1",
    "text": "Still a developer, with better tools.",
    "chapter": "SEGMENT 2: STAYING IN CONTROL (4 minutes)",
    "file": "0019.mp3",
    "duration": 2.856,
    "startTime": 123.716
  },
  {
    "index": 20,
    "dialogueIndex": 20,
    "rawLine": 70,
    "type": "dialogue",
    "speaker": "JAMIE",
    "voice": "F1",
    "text": "How do you use Claude for code review?",
    "chapter": "SEGMENT 3: CODE REVIEW WITH CLAUDE (3 minutes)",
    "file": "0020.mp3",
    "duration": 2.577,
    "startTime": 126.572
  },
  {
    "index": 21,
    "dialogueIndex": 21,
    "rawLine": 72,
    "type": "dialogue",
    "speaker": "ALEX",
    "voice": "M1",
    "text": "Before I submit a PR, I ask Claude to review my own changes. \"Review the changes I've made and point out any issues.\" It catches things I missed.",
    "chapter": "SEGMENT 3: CODE REVIEW WITH CLAUDE (3 minutes)",
    "file": "0021.mp3",
    "duration": 10.24,
    "startTime": 129.149
  },
  {
    "index": 22,
    "dialogueIndex": 22,
    "rawLine": 74,
    "type": "dialogue",
    "speaker": "JAMIE",
    "voice": "F1",
    "text": "Self-review with AI.",
    "chapter": "SEGMENT 3: CODE REVIEW WITH CLAUDE (3 minutes)",
    "file": "0022.mp3",
    "duration": 1.811,
    "startTime": 139.389
  },
  {
    "index": 23,
    "dialogueIndex": 23,
    "rawLine": 76,
    "type": "dialogue",
    "speaker": "ALEX",
    "voice": "M1",
    "text": "For reviewing others' code, I ask Claude to analyze the PR and highlight concerns. Then I do my own review, informed by Claude's analysis.",
    "chapter": "SEGMENT 3: CODE REVIEW WITH CLAUDE (3 minutes)",
    "file": "0023.mp3",
    "duration": 9.613,
    "startTime": 141.201
  },
  {
    "index": 24,
    "dialogueIndex": 24,
    "rawLine": 78,
    "type": "dialogue",
    "speaker": "JAMIE",
    "voice": "F1",
    "text": "Augmented review, not replaced review.",
    "chapter": "SEGMENT 3: CODE REVIEW WITH CLAUDE (3 minutes)",
    "file": "0024.mp3",
    "duration": 2.786,
    "startTime": 150.814
  },
  {
    "index": 25,
    "dialogueIndex": 25,
    "rawLine": 80,
    "type": "dialogue",
    "speaker": "ALEX",
    "voice": "M1",
    "text": "Right. Claude might catch technical issues, but you still need human judgment about design choices, maintainability, and fit with the broader system.",
    "chapter": "SEGMENT 3: CODE REVIEW WITH CLAUDE (3 minutes)",
    "file": "0025.mp3",
    "duration": 9.822,
    "startTime": 153.6
  },
  {
    "index": 26,
    "dialogueIndex": 26,
    "rawLine": 88,
    "type": "dialogue",
    "speaker": "JAMIE",
    "voice": "F1",
    "text": "How does Claude help you learn?",
    "chapter": "SEGMENT 4: LEARNING AND GROWING (4 minutes)",
    "file": "0026.mp3",
    "duration": 2.159,
    "startTime": 163.422
  },
  {
    "index": 27,
    "dialogueIndex": 27,
    "rawLine": 90,
    "type": "dialogue",
    "speaker": "ALEX",
    "voice": "M1",
    "text": "When I encounter unfamiliar code or concepts, I ask Claude to explain. \"Walk me through how this async iteration works.\" It's like having a patient tutor.",
    "chapter": "SEGMENT 4: LEARNING AND GROWING (4 minutes)",
    "file": "0027.mp3",
    "duration": 10.519,
    "startTime": 165.581
  },
  {
    "index": 28,
    "dialogueIndex": 28,
    "rawLine": 92,
    "type": "dialogue",
    "speaker": "JAMIE",
    "voice": "F1",
    "text": "Always available to teach.",
    "chapter": "SEGMENT 4: LEARNING AND GROWING (4 minutes)",
    "file": "0028.mp3",
    "duration": 2.229,
    "startTime": 176.1
  },
  {
    "index": 29,
    "dialogueIndex": 29,
    "rawLine": 94,
    "type": "dialogue",
    "speaker": "ALEX",
    "voice": "M1",
    "text": "I also use Claude when learning new technologies. \"I'm new to GraphQL. Explain the basics and how our project uses it.\" Personalized learning based on my actual codebase.",
    "chapter": "SEGMENT 4: LEARNING AND GROWING (4 minutes)",
    "file": "0029.mp3",
    "duration": 11.773,
    "startTime": 178.329
  },
  {
    "index": 30,
    "dialogueIndex": 30,
    "rawLine": 96,
    "type": "dialogue",
    "speaker": "JAMIE",
    "voice": "F1",
    "text": "Contextual learning.",
    "chapter": "SEGMENT 4: LEARNING AND GROWING (4 minutes)",
    "file": "0030.mp3",
    "duration": 1.811,
    "startTime": 190.102
  },
  {
    "index": 31,
    "dialogueIndex": 31,
    "rawLine": 98,
    "type": "dialogue",
    "speaker": "ALEX",
    "voice": "M1",
    "text": "And when Claude suggests something I don't understand, I always ask why. \"Why did you use this pattern instead of the obvious approach?\" The explanations teach me.",
    "chapter": "SEGMENT 4: LEARNING AND GROWING (4 minutes)",
    "file": "0031.mp3",
    "duration": 10.588,
    "startTime": 191.913
  },
  {
    "index": 32,
    "dialogueIndex": 32,
    "rawLine": 106,
    "type": "dialogue",
    "speaker": "JAMIE",
    "voice": "F1",
    "text": "How do you balance Claude and working with human teammates?",
    "chapter": "SEGMENT 5: EFFECTIVE COLLABORATION (3 minutes)",
    "file": "0032.mp3",
    "duration": 3.831,
    "startTime": 202.501
  },
  {
    "index": 33,
    "dialogueIndex": 33,
    "rawLine": 108,
    "type": "dialogue",
    "speaker": "ALEX",
    "voice": "M1",
    "text": "Claude helps me be a better teammate. I can draft PR descriptions with Claude before refining them myself. I can prepare for code reviews by understanding the code first.",
    "chapter": "SEGMENT 5: EFFECTIVE COLLABORATION (3 minutes)",
    "file": "0033.mp3",
    "duration": 11.564,
    "startTime": 206.333
  },
  {
    "index": 34,
    "dialogueIndex": 34,
    "rawLine": 110,
    "type": "dialogue",
    "speaker": "JAMIE",
    "voice": "F1",
    "text": "Preparation assistance.",
    "chapter": "SEGMENT 5: EFFECTIVE COLLABORATION (3 minutes)",
    "file": "0034.mp3",
    "duration": 2.02,
    "startTime": 217.896
  },
  {
    "index": 35,
    "dialogueIndex": 35,
    "rawLine": 112,
    "type": "dialogue",
    "speaker": "ALEX",
    "voice": "M1",
    "text": "When working on shared code, I'm more careful. I make sure Claude's changes align with team conventions, and I document why changes were made.",
    "chapter": "SEGMENT 5: EFFECTIVE COLLABORATION (3 minutes)",
    "file": "0035.mp3",
    "duration": 9.056,
    "startTime": 219.916
  },
  {
    "index": 36,
    "dialogueIndex": 36,
    "rawLine": 114,
    "type": "dialogue",
    "speaker": "JAMIE",
    "voice": "F1",
    "text": "Team awareness.",
    "chapter": "SEGMENT 5: EFFECTIVE COLLABORATION (3 minutes)",
    "file": "0036.mp3",
    "duration": 1.602,
    "startTime": 228.972
  },
  {
    "index": 37,
    "dialogueIndex": 37,
    "rawLine": 116,
    "type": "dialogue",
    "speaker": "ALEX",
    "voice": "M1",
    "text": "And I share what I learn. When Claude shows me a better pattern, I bring it to the team. The whole team can benefit from AI-assisted insights.",
    "chapter": "SEGMENT 5: EFFECTIVE COLLABORATION (3 minutes)",
    "file": "0037.mp3",
    "duration": 9.613,
    "startTime": 230.574
  },
  {
    "index": 38,
    "dialogueIndex": 38,
    "rawLine": 124,
    "type": "dialogue",
    "speaker": "JAMIE",
    "voice": "F1",
    "text": "Your best tips for debugging with Claude?",
    "chapter": "SEGMENT 6: DEBUGGING EFFICIENTLY (4 minutes)",
    "file": "0038.mp3",
    "duration": 2.647,
    "startTime": 240.187
  },
  {
    "index": 39,
    "dialogueIndex": 39,
    "rawLine": 126,
    "type": "dialogue",
    "speaker": "ALEX",
    "voice": "M1",
    "text": "Start with clear symptom description. The better you describe the problem, the faster Claude can help. Include error messages, reproduction steps, and what you've already tried.",
    "chapter": "SEGMENT 6: DEBUGGING EFFICIENTLY (4 minutes)",
    "file": "0039.mp3",
    "duration": 11.773,
    "startTime": 242.834
  },
  {
    "index": 40,
    "dialogueIndex": 40,
    "rawLine": 128,
    "type": "dialogue",
    "speaker": "JAMIE",
    "voice": "F1",
    "text": "Good bug reports for Claude.",
    "chapter": "SEGMENT 6: DEBUGGING EFFICIENTLY (4 minutes)",
    "file": "0040.mp3",
    "duration": 2.229,
    "startTime": 254.607
  },
  {
    "index": 41,
    "dialogueIndex": 41,
    "rawLine": 130,
    "type": "dialogue",
    "speaker": "ALEX",
    "voice": "M1",
    "text": "Let Claude investigate before jumping to conclusions. Sometimes the bug isn't where you think. Claude's systematic search can find the real cause.",
    "chapter": "SEGMENT 6: DEBUGGING EFFICIENTLY (4 minutes)",
    "file": "0041.mp3",
    "duration": 9.683,
    "startTime": 256.836
  },
  {
    "index": 42,
    "dialogueIndex": 42,
    "rawLine": 132,
    "type": "dialogue",
    "speaker": "JAMIE",
    "voice": "F1",
    "text": "Don't bias the investigation.",
    "chapter": "SEGMENT 6: DEBUGGING EFFICIENTLY (4 minutes)",
    "file": "0042.mp3",
    "duration": 2.09,
    "startTime": 266.519
  },
  {
    "index": 43,
    "dialogueIndex": 43,
    "rawLine": 134,
    "type": "dialogue",
    "speaker": "ALEX",
    "voice": "M1",
    "text": "And create a test that reproduces the bug before fixing it. Claude can help write this test. Then fixing becomes verifiable.",
    "chapter": "SEGMENT 6: DEBUGGING EFFICIENTLY (4 minutes)",
    "file": "0043.mp3",
    "duration": 8.22,
    "startTime": 268.608
  },
  {
    "index": 44,
    "dialogueIndex": 44,
    "rawLine": 136,
    "type": "dialogue",
    "speaker": "JAMIE",
    "voice": "F1",
    "text": "Test-confirmed fixes.",
    "chapter": "SEGMENT 6: DEBUGGING EFFICIENTLY (4 minutes)",
    "file": "0044.mp3",
    "duration": 1.881,
    "startTime": 276.828
  },
  {
    "index": 45,
    "dialogueIndex": 45,
    "rawLine": 144,
    "type": "dialogue",
    "speaker": "JAMIE",
    "voice": "F1",
    "text": "Is there a risk of becoming too dependent on Claude?",
    "chapter": "SEGMENT 7: AVOIDING OVER-RELIANCE (4 minutes)",
    "file": "0045.mp3",
    "duration": 3.483,
    "startTime": 278.709
  },
  {
    "index": 46,
    "dialogueIndex": 46,
    "rawLine": 146,
    "type": "dialogue",
    "speaker": "ALEX",
    "voice": "M1",
    "text": "It's worth being thoughtful about. Make sure you still understand the fundamentals. When Claude suggests a solution, understand why it works.",
    "chapter": "SEGMENT 7: AVOIDING OVER-RELIANCE (4 minutes)",
    "file": "0046.mp3",
    "duration": 9.474,
    "startTime": 282.192
  },
  {
    "index": 47,
    "dialogueIndex": 47,
    "rawLine": 148,
    "type": "dialogue",
    "speaker": "JAMIE",
    "voice": "F1",
    "text": "Keep your skills sharp.",
    "chapter": "SEGMENT 7: AVOIDING OVER-RELIANCE (4 minutes)",
    "file": "0047.mp3",
    "duration": 1.95,
    "startTime": 291.666
  },
  {
    "index": 48,
    "dialogueIndex": 48,
    "rawLine": 150,
    "type": "dialogue",
    "speaker": "ALEX",
    "voice": "M1",
    "text": "Occasionally do things the old way. Write code without Claude, debug by reading carefully, commit with hand-written messages. This keeps your skills from atrophying.",
    "chapter": "SEGMENT 7: AVOIDING OVER-RELIANCE (4 minutes)",
    "file": "0048.mp3",
    "duration": 11.215,
    "startTime": 293.616
  },
  {
    "index": 49,
    "dialogueIndex": 49,
    "rawLine": 152,
    "type": "dialogue",
    "speaker": "JAMIE",
    "voice": "F1",
    "text": "Practice without the assistant.",
    "chapter": "SEGMENT 7: AVOIDING OVER-RELIANCE (4 minutes)",
    "file": "0049.mp3",
    "duration": 2.368,
    "startTime": 304.832
  },
  {
    "index": 50,
    "dialogueIndex": 50,
    "rawLine": 154,
    "type": "dialogue",
    "speaker": "ALEX",
    "voice": "M1",
    "text": "And remember that Claude can be wrong. If something doesn't feel right, trust your instincts. You know your project better than Claude does.",
    "chapter": "SEGMENT 7: AVOIDING OVER-RELIANCE (4 minutes)",
    "file": "0050.mp3",
    "duration": 8.777,
    "startTime": 307.2
  },
  {
    "index": 51,
    "dialogueIndex": 51,
    "rawLine": 162,
    "type": "dialogue",
    "speaker": "JAMIE",
    "voice": "F1",
    "text": "How do you keep Claude Code efficient?",
    "chapter": "SEGMENT 8: PERFORMANCE AND EFFICIENCY (3 minutes)",
    "file": "0051.mp3",
    "duration": 2.577,
    "startTime": 315.977
  },
  {
    "index": 52,
    "dialogueIndex": 52,
    "rawLine": 164,
    "type": "dialogue",
    "speaker": "ALEX",
    "voice": "M1",
    "text": "Long conversations slow down. I use slash clear or slash compact regularly to keep things snappy.",
    "chapter": "SEGMENT 8: PERFORMANCE AND EFFICIENCY (3 minutes)",
    "file": "0052.mp3",
    "duration": 7.036,
    "startTime": 318.555
  },
  {
    "index": 53,
    "dialogueIndex": 53,
    "rawLine": 166,
    "type": "dialogue",
    "speaker": "JAMIE",
    "voice": "F1",
    "text": "Manage conversation length.",
    "chapter": "SEGMENT 8: PERFORMANCE AND EFFICIENCY (3 minutes)",
    "file": "0053.mp3",
    "duration": 2.159,
    "startTime": 325.59
  },
  {
    "index": 54,
    "dialogueIndex": 54,
    "rawLine": 168,
    "type": "dialogue",
    "speaker": "ALEX",
    "voice": "M1",
    "text": "I try to be specific about what I need. Narrow queries get faster responses than broad ones. \"Check only the auth module\" instead of \"search everywhere.\"",
    "chapter": "SEGMENT 8: PERFORMANCE AND EFFICIENCY (3 minutes)",
    "file": "0054.mp3",
    "duration": 10.937,
    "startTime": 327.75
  },
  {
    "index": 55,
    "dialogueIndex": 55,
    "rawLine": 170,
    "type": "dialogue",
    "speaker": "JAMIE",
    "voice": "F1",
    "text": "Focused requests.",
    "chapter": "SEGMENT 8: PERFORMANCE AND EFFICIENCY (3 minutes)",
    "file": "0055.mp3",
    "duration": 1.602,
    "startTime": 338.686
  },
  {
    "index": 56,
    "dialogueIndex": 56,
    "rawLine": 172,
    "type": "dialogue",
    "speaker": "ALEX",
    "voice": "M1",
    "text": "And I pay attention to what works. When a certain prompting style gets good results, I reuse it. Over time, you develop efficient patterns.",
    "chapter": "SEGMENT 8: PERFORMANCE AND EFFICIENCY (3 minutes)",
    "file": "0056.mp3",
    "duration": 9.474,
    "startTime": 340.288
  },
  {
    "index": 57,
    "dialogueIndex": 57,
    "rawLine": 180,
    "type": "dialogue",
    "speaker": "JAMIE",
    "voice": "F1",
    "text": "How do you build trust with Claude?",
    "chapter": "SEGMENT 9: BUILDING TRUST (3 minutes)",
    "file": "0057.mp3",
    "duration": 2.299,
    "startTime": 349.762
  },
  {
    "index": 58,
    "dialogueIndex": 58,
    "rawLine": 182,
    "type": "dialogue",
    "speaker": "ALEX",
    "voice": "M1",
    "text": "Start conservative. Require approval for everything at first. Review carefully. This builds your understanding of how Claude works.",
    "chapter": "SEGMENT 9: BUILDING TRUST (3 minutes)",
    "file": "0058.mp3",
    "duration": 9.404,
    "startTime": 352.061
  },
  {
    "index": 59,
    "dialogueIndex": 59,
    "rawLine": 184,
    "type": "dialogue",
    "speaker": "JAMIE",
    "voice": "F1",
    "text": "Start cautious.",
    "chapter": "SEGMENT 9: BUILDING TRUST (3 minutes)",
    "file": "0059.mp3",
    "duration": 1.602,
    "startTime": 361.465
  },
  {
    "index": 60,
    "dialogueIndex": 60,
    "rawLine": 186,
    "type": "dialogue",
    "speaker": "ALEX",
    "voice": "M1",
    "text": "As you see Claude succeed, relax restrictions. Allow read operations automatically. Trust more actions. But do this gradually.",
    "chapter": "SEGMENT 9: BUILDING TRUST (3 minutes)",
    "file": "0060.mp3",
    "duration": 9.543,
    "startTime": 363.067
  },
  {
    "index": 61,
    "dialogueIndex": 61,
    "rawLine": 188,
    "type": "dialogue",
    "speaker": "JAMIE",
    "voice": "F1",
    "text": "Earn expanded trust.",
    "chapter": "SEGMENT 9: BUILDING TRUST (3 minutes)",
    "file": "0061.mp3",
    "duration": 1.881,
    "startTime": 372.611
  },
  {
    "index": 62,
    "dialogueIndex": 62,
    "rawLine": 190,
    "type": "dialogue",
    "speaker": "ALEX",
    "voice": "M1",
    "text": "And if Claude makes a mistake, understand why. Was the prompt unclear? Did you give bad context? Learning from mistakes makes future interactions better.",
    "chapter": "SEGMENT 9: BUILDING TRUST (3 minutes)",
    "file": "0062.mp3",
    "duration": 10.449,
    "startTime": 374.491
  },
  {
    "index": 63,
    "dialogueIndex": 63,
    "rawLine": 198,
    "type": "dialogue",
    "speaker": "JAMIE",
    "voice": "F1",
    "text": "Does code organization matter for Claude effectiveness?",
    "chapter": "SEGMENT 10: PROJECT ORGANIZATION FOR AI (3 minutes)",
    "file": "0063.mp3",
    "duration": 3.901,
    "startTime": 384.94
  },
  {
    "index": 64,
    "dialogueIndex": 64,
    "rawLine": 200,
    "type": "dialogue",
    "speaker": "ALEX",
    "voice": "M1",
    "text": "Absolutely. Clear, well-organized code is easier for Claude to understand. Good naming, logical structure, consistent patterns.",
    "chapter": "SEGMENT 10: PROJECT ORGANIZATION FOR AI (3 minutes)",
    "file": "0064.mp3",
    "duration": 9.334,
    "startTime": 388.841
  },
  {
    "index": 65,
    "dialogueIndex": 65,
    "rawLine": 202,
    "type": "dialogue",
    "speaker": "JAMIE",
    "voice": "F1",
    "text": "Good code practices help AI too.",
    "chapter": "SEGMENT 10: PROJECT ORGANIZATION FOR AI (3 minutes)",
    "file": "0065.mp3",
    "duration": 2.577,
    "startTime": 398.176
  },
  {
    "index": 66,
    "dialogueIndex": 66,
    "rawLine": 204,
    "type": "dialogue",
    "speaker": "ALEX",
    "voice": "M1",
    "text": "Documentation matters. Claude reads your comments, your README, your CLAUDE.md. Good documentation makes Claude more effective.",
    "chapter": "SEGMENT 10: PROJECT ORGANIZATION FOR AI (3 minutes)",
    "file": "0066.mp3",
    "duration": 9.474,
    "startTime": 400.753
  },
  {
    "index": 67,
    "dialogueIndex": 67,
    "rawLine": 206,
    "type": "dialogue",
    "speaker": "JAMIE",
    "voice": "F1",
    "text": "Document for humans and AI.",
    "chapter": "SEGMENT 10: PROJECT ORGANIZATION FOR AI (3 minutes)",
    "file": "0067.mp3",
    "duration": 2.159,
    "startTime": 410.227
  },
  {
    "index": 68,
    "dialogueIndex": 68,
    "rawLine": 208,
    "type": "dialogue",
    "speaker": "ALEX",
    "voice": "M1",
    "text": "And keep related code together. If your auth logic is scattered across ten folders, Claude has to work harder. Cohesive organization helps everyone.",
